course: dictionary
lesson: 2900
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. «Dove» is one of them: it can be a bird, a sign of peace, or the past tense of dive. To find the right meaning, read the words around it. Those words are the context, and they leave clues.
explain: «The white dove flew over the town.» The clues are white and flew, so dove means a bird here. «She dove into the pool.» The clue is the pool, and the word is in the past tense, so dove means went down into the water. Ask yourself which meaning fits the sentence.
explain: A dove is also a sign of peace. When someone talks about «a dove of peace», they mean peace, not a bird. In politics, a person who wants peace rather than war is called a dove.
explain: People in different countries can use the same word in different ways. In the USA and Canada, children say «dove» for the past of dive. In the UK, they usually say «dived». Both are correct in their own places.
fact: A dove is a pale grey or white bird of the pigeon family that coos.
fact: Doves and pigeons are in the same family, so city pigeons are related to wild rock doves.
fact: A dove is a sign of peace, and the dove and the olive branch became symbols of peace and new beginnings.
fact: In the USA and Canada, «dove» (rhymes with stove) is the past tense of dive, as in «She dove into the pool.»
exercise: «The white dove flew over the town.» What is a dove in this sentence? | A sign of anger | A type of cake | *A bird | A fast car
exercise: «She dove into the pool.» What does dove mean here? | Sat beside the pool | Ran away from the pool | Cried by the pool | *Went down into the water, the past of dive
exercise: Someone says «a dove of peace». What does dove mean? | A loud argument | *A sign of peace | A grey, wet day | A dish of rice
test: The dove and the olive branch became symbols of what? | Speed | Anger and war | Hunger | *Peace and new beginnings
test: In the UK, what do children usually say as the past of dive? | Dives | *Dived | Diving | Dove
exam: Which sentence uses dove as the past tense of dive? | The dove sat on the wire. | *Tom dove off the diving board. | A dove is a kind of bird. | We saw a dove of peace.
